{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1468632-advice-for-a-rookie-st","id":1468632,"title":"Advice for a Rookie ST?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-22T14:04:44-08:00","id":1468632,"title":"Advice for a Rookie ST?","content":"TL;DR - Advice for a new Wraith ST?<br /> <br /> So I've been running VTM for about 5-6 years now, reading up on the books before that. I've also tried my hand with Werewolf running a short chronicle of that set in California. I'd really like to try my hand at running Wraith, I've watched Huddyvonschland's Wraith Lore series, the new videos from Lore by Night, and the short game that Matthew Dawkins ran. I've also been going through the Wraith 20 book when I get the chance.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested in any advice for a newbie Wraith ST:<br /> - Any particular pitfalls I should be aware of as an ST? (Mechanical, plot or lore-wise, general TTRPG etiquette-wise, etc.)<br /> - Any particular character-building advice? (My players have all played in my WoD games before, but we've never done Wraith.)<br /> - Any resources I should look at outside of the corebook?<br /> - Any particular themes I should present or engage with?<br /> - Any particular elements of lore I need to include or present to the players? (Especially for first time players.)<br /> - Any particular suggestions for what a short intro chronicle might focus on?<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance to everyone who takes the time, it's very much appreciated. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T07:49:10-08:00","id":1468686,"title":"","content":"A lot of it depends on what parts of Wraith you want to follow up on. Are you going to focus on wraith society? On personal connections to the Skinlands? On Stygia? <br /> <br /> Beyond that, my big piece of advice is be careful with shadowguiding. It's a situation where characters have to share control (and creative control) and it's a situation that bears a similarity to real mental issues. Its a fun mechanic but it can get off the rails fairly quickly if players aren't on the same page or spend too much time on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T14:30:23-08:00","id":1468780,"title":"","content":"My intent is very much crash-course Wraith. You're dead, here's what happens next type of deal, to showcase the game/setting to my players.<br /> <br /> RE: The Shadow, what're the general guides with that? My understanding is another player tends to portray your shadow and they're simply put a dark self-destructive side to the Wraith. How much time/power should be given over to the Shadows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T20:56:19-08:00","id":1468812,"title":"","content":"In that kind of game I\u2019d put the focus on the personal side of the wraithly condition. I\u2019d use Passions and Fetters and whatever else drives the characters to push them up against their limitations and complicate their afterlives. I\u2019d leave wraith society as a secondary element that either helps or hinders the primary goal. <br /> <br /> As for the shadow, I think the recommendation is that playing a Shadow should take no more than 10% of a player\u2019s time. <br /> <br /> The dangerous thing about the Shadow is that it is a part of someone else\u2019s character. This isn\u2019t like the Beast or the Thrall of the Wyrm; it\u2019s not an alien force that influences or takes over the character. The Shadow, though twisted, is an actual part of the character, so the Shadowguide and the Player really need to be on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}